course: dictionary
lesson: 3248
title: The outer layer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Epidermis is a science word. Its meaning is the thin outer layer of the skin that you can see and touch. Read the context to find clues: «the outer epidermis» tells you it is on the outside, and «protects» tells you its job.
explain: «The outer layer has no blood vessels, so a very light scrape does not bleed.» Blood vessels are in the layer underneath, so a light scrape that stays in the outer layer does not bleed. The clue is in the sentence, and that is how you check your meaning.
explain: The same word is used for plants. A leaf has an epidermis too, which is the outer layer of cells on a leaf, stem or root. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «outer layer» fits, you are on the right track.
fact: Epidermis is a noun, a word for a thing.
fact: «Epidermis» means the thin outer layer of the skin that you can see and touch.
fact: The epidermis protects the body from germs, water and sunlight.
fact: The epidermis sits on top of the dermis, which has blood vessels and nerves.
fact: In plants, «epidermis» means the outer layer of cells on a leaf, stem or root.
exercise: «The outer epidermis protects the body.» What does epidermis mean here? | The bones that hold you up | The blood inside the body | *The thin outer layer of the skin | The fat layer under the skin
exercise: In plant lessons, what is the epidermis? | The inside of a seed | *The outer layer of cells on a leaf, stem or root | The water that roots drink | The sun's heat on a leaf
exercise: «The outer layer has no blood vessels, so a very light scrape does not bleed.» Find and copy one word that names this outer layer. | fat | blood | dermis | *epidermis
test: What job does the epidermis do? | Makes the bones strong | *Protects the body from germs, water and sunlight | Pumps blood around the body | Stores fat for winter
test: Why does a very light scrape not bleed? | Blood only flows in the fat layer | *The outer layer has no blood vessels | The scrape is always dry | The skin is too thick to cut
exam: Sunburn damages which layer of the skin? | *The epidermis | The fat layer | The bones | The dermis
